dcmR — Acknowledgment of upstream sources
=========================================

The dcmR package is an R port of routines originally implemented in the
MATLAB SPM12 toolbox (Statistical Parametric Mapping), distributed by the
Wellcome Centre for Human Neuroimaging, University College London, under
the GNU General Public License version 2 (GPL-2).

The following dcmR functions are direct ports (with optimizations) of the
corresponding SPM12 MATLAB routines. The mapping uses the dcmR convention
of replacing the 'spm_' prefix with 'dcm_' (and collapsing the redundant
'spm_dcm_' prefix to a single 'dcm_').

  dcmR function              SPM12 original
  -------------              --------------
  dcm_estimate               spm_dcm_estimate
  dcm_fmri_priors            spm_dcm_fmri_priors
  dcm_fmri_mode_gen          spm_dcm_fmri_mode_gen
  dcm_evidence               spm_dcm_evidence
  dcm_nlsi_GN                spm_nlsi_GN
  dcm_int                    spm_int
  dcm_bireduce               spm_bireduce
  dcm_kernels                spm_kernels
  dcm_fx_fmri                spm_fx_fmri
  dcm_fx_fmri2               spm_fx_fmri (analytic-Jacobian variant)
  dcm_gx_fmri                spm_gx_fmri
  dcm_diff                   spm_diff
  dcm_dx                     spm_dx
  dcm_expm                   spm_expm
  dcm_Ce                     spm_Ce
  dcm_Q                      spm_Q
  dcm_logdet                 spm_logdet
  dcm_inv                    spm_inv
  dcm_pinv                   spm_pinv
  dcm_svd                    spm_svd
  dcm_cat                    spm_cat
  dcm_diag                   spm_diag
  dcm_vec                    spm_vec
  dcm_unvec                  spm_unvec
  dcm_length                 spm_length
  dcm_zeros                  spm_zeros
  dcm_en                     spm_en
  dcm_detrend                spm_detrend
  dcm_speye                  spm_speye
  dcm_phi                    spm_phi
  dcm_Ncdf                   spm_Ncdf
  dcm_data_id                spm_data_id
  dcm_funcheck               spm_funcheck
  dcm_log_evidence           spm_log_evidence
  dcm_log_evidence_reduce    spm_log_evidence_reduce
  dcm_fieldindices           spm_fieldindices
  dcm_find_pC                spm_find_pC
  dcm_find_rC                spm_find_rC
  dcm_trace                  spm_trace
  dcm_blocks_to_mat          (helper added in dcmR)

The Krylov-projection helper expv() and the Pade-approximation helper
padm() are direct ports of the corresponding SPM12 utilities and retain
their original names.

We thank the SPM12 authors and the Wellcome Centre for Human Neuroimaging
for making the original implementation freely available under GPL-2. The
R port inherits the GPL-2 license.

References
----------

Friston, K.J., Harrison, L., Penny, W. (2003). Dynamic causal modelling.
NeuroImage, 19(4), 1273-1302.

Friston, K.J., Mattout, J., Trujillo-Barreto, N., Ashburner, J., Penny, W.
(2007). Variational free energy and the Laplace approximation. NeuroImage,
34(1), 220-234.

SPM12 software: https://www.fil.ion.ucl.ac.uk/spm/software/spm12/
